.playwright-mcp/

# Rocq extraction output from formal/codegen-ptx/extraction/Extract.v.
#
# `Extraction Library` writes these to the project root, and every proof run
# rewrites them, so tracking them meant a dirty tree after each `make -f
# CoqMakefile`. They were tracked for a long time anyway, and were dead weight
# the whole time: they do not compile as they stand (they open Datatypes/List/
# Nat, modules that exist only if the Stdlib is extracted alongside them), no
# dune stanza names them, and no gate diffs them -- so unlike
# extraction/sarek_ptx_layout_model.ml, which IS linked and IS byte-compared by
# scripts/check-formal-proofs.sh, a committed copy proved nothing.
#
# Extract.v itself stays in the build: compiling it asserts the theories remain
# extractable. Migrating these five modules to the self-contained
# `Extraction "file.ml"` form that the layout model uses -- and then linking
# them, which is what would let the conformance suite test the extracted model
# instead of its own transcription -- is separate work (backlog-187).
/formal/codegen-ptx/AGpuSemantics.ml
/formal/codegen-ptx/AGpuSemantics.mli
/formal/codegen-ptx/PtxExprSpec.ml
/formal/codegen-ptx/PtxExprSpec.mli
/formal/codegen-ptx/PtxKernelSpec.ml
/formal/codegen-ptx/PtxKernelSpec.mli
/formal/codegen-ptx/PtxStmtSpec.ml
/formal/codegen-ptx/PtxStmtSpec.mli
/formal/codegen-ptx/PtxTypes.ml
/formal/codegen-ptx/PtxTypes.mli
